- Description: Register new user and obtain a public profile_id
- Action: POST /register with body {"email":"alice@example.com","password":"pass1234"}
- Expected behavior: Status code 201. Response body is JSON containing "profile_id" with a non-empty string value.

- Description: Login with valid credentials returns token and profile_id
- Action: POST /login with body {"email":"alice@example.com","password":"pass1234"}
- Expected behavior: Status 200, JSON body contains "token" (non-empty string) and "profile_id" (non-empty string matching the one from registration).

- Description: Login with wrong password fails
- Action: POST /login with body {"email":"alice@example.com","password":"wrong"}
- Expected behavior: Status 4xx.

- Description: Submit report with authenticated user returns coarse location and report fields
- Action: Register a user (e.g., alice@example.com), login to obtain token and profile_id. Then POST /reports with Authorization: Bearer <token> and body {"category":"pothole","description":"Large pothole","latitude":40.7128,"longitude":-74.0060}
- Expected behavior: 201 status. Response JSON includes "id" (non-empty string), "category":"pothole", "description":"Large pothole", "neighborhood" (non-empty string), "profile_id" matching the authenticated user's profile_id, and "created_at" (a string representing ISO 8601 datetime).

- Description: Submit report with an invalid access token fails
- Action: POST /reports with header Authorization: Bearer faketoken and body {"category":"pothole","description":"desc","latitude":40.0,"longitude":-74.0}
- Expected behavior: Status 4xx.

